+## Browser build for pages (`wasm/build-web.sh`)
+
+`wasm/build-web.sh [BUILD_DIR]` relinks the runtime (no recompilation) into
+`BUILD_DIR/bin-web` for use from a web page:
+
+* modular (`createOoRexx` factory), hosted in a dedicated Web Worker
+  (`web/ooRexx-worker.js`): one fresh interpreter per run, the page never
+  blocks, and terminating the worker stops the run and all its threads;
+* interactive standard input: `read()` of fd 0 is wrapped
+  (`-Wl,--wrap=read`, `web-stdin.cpp`) and served on the calling pthread from
+  a ring in shared memory that the main runtime thread fills when the page
+  sends input (`web-pre.js`); `LINES()`/`CHARS()` see what is buffered;
+* standard output and error as raw bytes, so a `CHAROUT` prompt shows before
+  the program waits;
+* what the interpreter writes is marked for the page: trace lines (an error's
+  traceback included) and error messages, wherever `.traceOutput` sends them,
+  and whether a read is interactive trace's (`.debugInput`).  `Activity.cpp`
+  calls a weak hook, `orx_wasm_mark()`, defined only by this build
+  (`web-stdin.cpp`); the marks live in the shared stdin ring, where
+  `web-pre.js` reads them as the bytes are written or the input is requested;
+* the portable extension classes preloaded in `/usr/lib/ooRexx` (`REXX_PATH`);
+* `Atomics.waitAsync` hidden (`web-pre.js`): WebKit sometimes loses its
+  wakeups, and Emscripten uses it to tell a thread that work was proxied to
+  it (the interpreter's system calls go to the runtime's thread, where MEMFS
+  lives), which left ~5-10% of runs hanging; without it Emscripten notifies
+  by postMessage;
+* `Date.now()` with the resolution of `performance.now()` (`web-pre.js`), so
+  that MEMFS stamps files with the interpreter's clock (a file written now no
+  longer looks older than the moment it was written at); MEMFS still reads
+  file times back in whole milliseconds (its `stat()` goes through a JS Date);
+* `.RexxInfo~libraryPath` is `/usr/lib/ooRexx/`, the directory of the
+  preloaded classes; `.RexxInfo~executable` is .nil: the executable
+  (`rexx.wasm`, `rexx.js`) was loaded from a URL, or the browser's cache,
+  not from the program's file system, so there is no File to give for it.
+
+The page API is `web/ooRexx.js`:
+
+```js
+const rexx = await OoRexx.load();       // compiles rexx.wasm, fetches rexx.data once
+const run = rexx.run({ args: ['prog.rex'], files: {'/home/rexx/prog.rex': src},
+                       onOut, onErr, onInput });
+run.write('line\n'); run.close();       // interactive stdin; or stdin: '...' up front
+run.stop();
+const { rc, files, stopped, ms } = await run.done;
+// onOut(text, kind), onErr(text, kind): kind is 'trace', 'error' (an error
+// message) or 'plain'; onInput({debug}): debug when .debugInput is reading
+```
+
+`wasm/tests/web-api.html` is a minimal page over it. The page must be cross-origin
+isolated (see above).  `wasm/tests/web-api.py BIN_WEB` runs assertions over the
+API in headless Chromium (Python Playwright): output, interactive and fixed
+stdin, EOF, stop, threads, files in and out, extension classes, rexxtry,
+trace and error marks, debug input.
+
 ## Known limitations / deliberate non-claims
 
 * WebSocket transport (browser, and the MEMFS build under Node): listening
