+ * thread, which wasm/web/ooRexx-worker.js puts in a dedicated Web Worker.
+ *
+ *  - standard output and error as raw bytes (Module.orxOut / Module.orxErr,
+ *    batched per task), not as lines: a prompt written with CHAROUT must
+ *    show before the program waits for input.  Each batch says what the
+ *    interpreter was writing ('plain', 'trace' or 'error' for an error
+ *    message), as marked by its orx_wasm_mark hook (wasm/web-stdin.cpp);
+ *  - the producer side of the standard input ring of wasm/web-stdin.cpp:
+ *    Module.orxStdinWrite(bytes), Module.orxStdinClose(); the program asking
+ *    for input calls Module.orxStdinWanted(debug) (set by the worker), debug
+ *    being true when the read is interactive trace's (.debugInput);
+ *  - ioctl(0, FIONREAD) answers the bytes the program can read without
+ *    waiting, so LINES() and CHARS() on STDIN work;
+ *  - REXX_PATH points at the preloaded extension classes;
+ *  - Atomics.waitAsync is hidden (see below).
