+
+// WebKit (Safari 26) sometimes loses an Atomics.waitAsync wakeup.  Emscripten
+// uses waitAsync to tell a thread that work was proxied to it, above all the
+// interpreter thread's system calls to the main runtime thread (MEMFS lives
+// there): a lost wakeup leaves the run hanging for good, in ~5-10% of runs
